Introduction:
This project aims to check whether all the required details are provided by a customer before booking a flight.
Sometimes customers may forget to mention important information such as travel date, number of passengers, or travel class. 
Using prompt engineering, the system identifies the available details, finds the missing information, and asks the customer 
to provide it. This helps make the flight booking process easier and avoids incomplete bookings.

Prompt:
Read the customer's message carefully and identify the flight booking details provided. Check whether all the
required information is available, including Passenger Name, Departure City, Destination City, Travel Date, Number of 
Passengers, and Travel Class.
Display the available information and mark any missing field as Missing.
If some details are missing, ask the customer to provide only those missing details. 
Do not guess or assume any information that the customer has not provided.

Sample Inputs and Expected Outputs

1. Input:
My name is Priya. I need a flight from Mumbai to Chennai on 15 December 2026 for two passengers in Economy class.

Passenger Name: Priya
Departure City: Mumbai
Destination City: Chennai
Travel Date: 15 December 2026
Number of Passengers: 2
Travel Class: Economy

2. Input:
I am Arjun. I want to travel from Hyderabad to Pune.

Expected Output:
Passenger Name: Arjun
Departure City: Hyderabad
Destination City: Pune
Travel Date: Missing
Number of Passengers: Missing
Travel Class: Missing

